hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17880","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Mirdas al-Aslami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The righteous will be taken, the first then the first, and there will remain like the dregs of dates."
"17881","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us: Qays narrated to me, he said: I heard Mirdas al-Aslami, he said: The righteous will be taken, the first then the first, until there remains like the dregs of dates or barley; Allah will not care about them at all."
"17882","Ya'la narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Mirdas al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous will be taken, the first then the first, until there remains like the dregs of dates or barley; Allah will not care about them at all."
